/-!
# `lim ℱ/𝓘ⁿℱ` is derived complete, and the canonical comparison from `ℱ^∧`

Let `X` be a locally Noetherian scheme, `𝓘 ⊂ 𝒪_X` a quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals and `ℱ` a
coherent `𝒪_X`-module. This file proves that the **ordinary** inverse limit `lim ℱ/𝓘ⁿℱ`, placed in
degree zero, is derived complete along `𝓘` in the sense of [Stacks, Tag 0999], and deduces that
there is a unique map

`ℱ^∧ ⟶ (lim ℱ/𝓘ⁿℱ)[0]`

compatible with the completion unit `ℱ ⟶ ℱ^∧` and the canonical map `ℱ ⟶ lim ℱ/𝓘ⁿℱ`. Nothing is
assumed beyond the hypotheses of [Stacks, Tag 0A0K]: the scheme is not asked to be quasi-compact
and the ideal sheaf is not asked to be generated by global sections.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.existsUnique_derivedCompletionUnit_comp` — the maps `K^∧ ⟶ N`
  into a derived-complete `N` are in bijection with the maps `K ⟶ N`, by composition with the
  unit.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.pow_mem_idealPowerMultiple_unit` — the `n`-th power of a section of
  `𝓘` is a section of `𝓘ⁿ𝒪_X`, over an **arbitrary** open.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.sectionKills_pow_adicQuotientSystem_obj` — for a section `a` of `𝓘` over
  an open `V`, the power `aⁿ` annihilates `ℱ/𝓘ⁿℱ` over every open of `V`.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.isDerivedComplete_single_adicQuotientSystem_obj` — each term of the adic
  quotient tower, in degree zero, is derived complete along `𝓘`.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.isDerivedComplete_single_limit_adicQuotientSystem` — **`lim ℱ/𝓘ⁿℱ`,
  placed in degree zero, is derived complete along `𝓘`.**
* `Stacks.Algebraization.existsUnique_comparison_derivedCompletion_limit_adicQuotientSystem` —
  **the canonical comparison `ℱ^∧ ⟶ (lim ℱ/𝓘ⁿℱ)[0]`**, as the unique map compatible with the two
  units.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A0K](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A0K)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0999](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0999)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 099F](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099F)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 099Q](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099Q)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08FJ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08FJ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A0F](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A0F)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CQH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CQH)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite TopologicalSpace
